<!-- GENERATED FILE — edit templates/index.html.jinja + data/overview.json, then rerun scripts/generate_pages.py -->
{% from "_nav.html.jinja" import render_nav %}
{% from "_units.html.jinja" import unit %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Pacific Coast Bike Tour — Los Altos to Los Angeles</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/main.css">
  <meta name="description" content="An {{ total_days }}-day, {{ stats.distance_mi }}+ mile bike tour down the California coast from Los Altos to Los Angeles, {{ trip_dates }}.">

  <link rel="icon" href="icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#F2EFE9">
  <script>
    try {
      if (localStorage.getItem("pcgf-units") === "metric") document.documentElement.classList.add("metric");
    } catch (e) {}
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
    integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="">
</head>

<body>

  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

  <div class="top-band">
    <header>
      <h1 class="site-title"><a href="index.html">Pacific Coast Bike Tour</a></h1>
      <p class="site-tagline">The "LA to LA" ride: Los Altos to Los Angeles.</p>
    </header>

    {{ render_nav('home') }}
  </div>

  <main id="main">

    <div class="day-title">
      <div class="day-title__number">
        <span class="day-title__label">{{ total_days }} days &middot; {{ trip_dates }}</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="day-title__route town-route">
        <span class="town-name">Los Altos</span>
        <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="town-name">Los Angeles</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    

    <div class="stat-row overview-stats">
      <dl class="stat-item">
        <dt class="stat-label">Distance mapped</dt>
        <dd class="stat-value">{{ unit(stats.distance_mi, 'mi', stats.distance_km, 'km') }}</dd>
      </dl>
      <dl class="stat-item">
        <dt class="stat-label">Elevation gain</dt>
        <dd class="stat-value">{{ unit(stats.gain_ft, 'ft', stats.gain_m, 'm') }}</dd>
      </dl>
      <dl class="stat-item">
        <dt class="stat-label">Riding days</dt>
        <dd class="stat-value">{{ known_days }}<span class="stat-unit">of {{ total_days }} mapped</span></dd>
      </dl>
      <dl class="stat-item">
        <dt class="stat-label">Riders</dt>
        <dd class="stat-value">{{ riders|length }}<span class="stat-unit">+ {{ sag|length }} SAG</span></dd>
      </dl>
      <button type="button" class="unit-toggle" id="unit-toggle" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Toggle between imperial and metric units">
        <span class="unit-toggle__option" data-unit="imperial">mi</span>
        <span class="unit-toggle__option" data-unit="metric">km</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="route-section route-section--single">
      <figure class="map-card">
        <div id="map" class="map-card__map" role="region" aria-label="Map of the mapped days of the route, Los Altos toward Los Angeles"></div>
        <figcaption class="map-card__caption">Days 1&ndash;5 and 7&ndash;8 as currently mapped. Day 6 (Oceano to Santa Barbara) is still being planned.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-heading">Day by day</h2>
    <div class="day-grid">
      {% for d in days %}
      <a class="day-card{% if d.pending %} day-card--pending{% endif %}" href="day-{{ d.day }}.html">
        <div class="day-card__body">
          <div class="day-card__number">
            <span>Day {{ d.day }}</span>
            <span class="day-card__date">{{ d.date_label }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="day-card__route">
            {{ d.towns.start }} <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> {{ d.towns.end }}
          </div>
          {% if d.pending %}
          <div class="day-card__stat day-card__stat--pending">Route TBD</div>
          {% else %}
          <div class="day-card__stat">{{ unit(d.distance_mi, 'mi', d.distance_km, 'km') }} &middot; {{ unit(d.gain_ft, 'ft', d.gain_m, 'm') }} gain</div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p>Eight of us are riding California's Pacific Coast this September, traveling from Los Altos to Los Angeles over eight days, September 5 to 12, 2026. Following one of the most scenic cycling routes in North America, we'll climb coastal headlands, descend into seaside towns, and cover the route one day at a time.</p>

    <p>The tour is hotel-based, allowing us to travel light. A minimally supported SAG vehicle, driven by two of our spouses, transports our luggage between overnight stops while carrying ride essentials such as snacks, water, and morale boosts.</p>

    <p>This site documents the journey, including the route, daily stages, elevation profiles leading up to our departure. Ride photos to come soon.</p>

    <p>A self-supported bike tour down the California coast, loosely inspired by Adventure Cycling's Pacific Coast route &mdash; see how our planned days line up against it on the <a href="compare.html">route comparison page</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Who's riding</h2>
    <div class="roster">
      <div class="roster-group">
        <h3 class="roster-group__label">Riders</h3>
        <ul class="roster-list" role="list">
          {% for name in riders %}
          <li>{{ name }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="roster-group">
        <h3 class="roster-group__label">SAG car</h3>
        <ul class="roster-list" role="list">
          {% for name in sag %}
          <li>{{ name }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>

  <script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
    integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script>
    window.__days = {{ days_json|safe }};
  </script>
  <script src="js/map.js"></script>
  <script src="js/units.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
